{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg8p4p3tgHDHWxVFtnXik","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ERFxKrmeQn2GCU29fDkKkk","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> src/engine/AGENTS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## `audio-metadata.js`\n\n`readAudioMetadata(file, torrentPath, options, parser)` is the only\nplace the engine hands `music-metadata` a file. An unfinished file is\nparsed from `file.createReadStream()`, and that stream holds a piece\nbuffer and a high-priority selection until it is destroyed -- the\nlibrary stops reading once it has what it needs but never destroys the\nstream it was given. So the module owns the stream and destroys it once\nthe parse settles, either way. Finished files go through `parseFile`,\nwhich closes its own file. Do not call `mm.parseStream` from `index.js`\nagain: `test/unit/engine-audio-metadata-wiring.js` scans for exactly\nthat. `parser` defaults to `music-metadata` and is a parameter so\n`test/unit/engine-audio-metadata.js` can drive a real `Readable`\nwithout audio.\nEOF\nnpm test > /tmp/wtd-04-test.log 2>&1; echo exit=$?; grep -E \"^# (tests|pass|fail)\" /tmp/wtd-04-test.log; grep -n \"^not ok\" /tmp/wtd-04-test.log | head"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":293,"cache_read_input_tokens":64416,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":293},"output_tokens":67,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14673048-cc01-4d4d-9fd7-2a2cca52022a","uuid":"084516f5-351f-4fcf-900d-ac2990e43589","timestamp":"2026-10-18T01:11:20.725Z","request_id":"req_011Cg8p4oJzEY9juCGGtVhec","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01ERFxKrmeQn2GCU29fDkKkk":{"command":"cat >> src/engine/AGENTS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## `