{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg8p8dhegbdxpSWBsZGkc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Changing audio tracks on a file that is still downloading no longer leaves a stream open. The full `npm test` passes (4268/4268, lint clean), and everything is committed in three commits except the notes file.\n\n**What changed:**\n1. A new module, `src/engine/audio-metadata.js`, exports `readAudioMetadata(file, torrentPath, options, parser = mm)`. For an unfinished file it opens the torrent read stream, passes it to the parser, and destroys it when the parse finishes, whether it succeeded or failed. Finished files still use `parseFile` on the path on disk.\n2. In `src/engine/index.js`, `getAudioMetadata` now goes through that module, and the engine no longer imports `music-metadata` directly. The `wt-audio-metadata` replies are unchanged, and a failed parse is still only logged, with no reply.\n\n**Tests** (each one failed before the code that makes it pass was written):\n1. `test/unit/engine-audio-metadata.js` uses a real Node `Readable` and a stand-in parser passed in through the `parser` argument. It checks that the stream is destroyed after a successful parse and after a failed one, that it stays open while the parse is still running, and that a finished file is read from disk without opening a stream.\n2. `test/unit/engine-audio-metadata-wiring.js` scans the source of `index.js`. It checks that the handler calls `readAudioMetadata` and that nothing in the engine calls `parseStream` or `createReadStream()` directly. The ticket suggested `engine-torrent-close-wiring.js` for this, but that file doesn't exist on this branch yet, so I wrote a separate file instead.\n\nI also added an `audio-metadata.js` section to `src/engine/AGENTS.md`, and my notes are in `.nightralph/notes.md`, which isn't committed.\n\n[x] The stream is destroyed after a parse that resolves\n[x] The stream is destroyed after a parse that rejects\n[x] `wt-get-audio-metadata` reads through the new module (source scan)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":417,"cache_read_input_tokens":65259,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":417},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14673048-cc01-4d4d-9fd7-2a2cca52022a","uuid":"17de41c9-09ab-4cee-985c-ed0d17f5d56d","timestamp":"2026-10-18T01:12:15.787Z","request_id":"req_011Cg8p8dSn35CByByBgBcJo"}
